ANDROID-FINAL-STACK-2 — the incident that looked exactly like a broken cell
=========================================================================
Reproduced twice on package dev.selfhost.app (a name reused from
ANDROID-FINAL-STACK-1, which ran against a different engine).

  [FATAL:flutter/runtime/dart_vm_initializer.cc(88)] Error while initializing
  the Dart VM: Wrong full snapshot version,
    expected '21139db2770724220da55c72db00acdc'
    found    '839937ddd3133a1c0758aeeefce5448c'
  Fatal signal 6 (SIGABRT) ... io.flutter.embedding.engine.FlutterJNI.performNativeAttach

WHICH VERSION IS WHOSE — measured, not inferred:
  21139db2…  cell f85251f3… arm64 libflutter.so : 1 occurrence   <- OURS
  21139db2…  the APK's libapp.so                : 2 occurrences  <- OURS
  839937dd…  fallback 69f9831c arm64 libflutter.so : 1 occurrence <- FALLBACK
So the engine was ours and the SNAPSHOT IT LOADED was the fallback lineage's.

WHY, and it is not the cell:
  A first launch after `adb uninstall` + `install -r` logged
    current_patch_number: Some(1)
    Prepared boot of patch 1
    active path: .../files/shorebird_updater/patches/1/dlc.vmcode
  200 ms after install, on a data directory that `ls -d /data/data/<pkg>`
  confirms an uninstall removes. Android's backup manager had restored
  files/shorebird_updater/ from the EARLIER same-package app -- a patch
  inflated for a different engine.

PROOF: with `adb shell bmgr enable false`, the same APK and the same patch gave
    No existing state file found ... creating new state
    current_patch_number: None
    Patch successfully applied ... output_written=2884496b
    Update thread finished with status: Update installed
Nothing about the cell, the engine or the patch changed between those two runs.

FIXED AT THE ROOT: a lane-specific org (dev.selfhost.afs2), so the package name
cannot collide with another lane's app data.
MADE DETECTABLE: afs2_device.sh disables the backup manager for the run and
asserts the updater's own "No existing state file found" and
"current_patch_number: None" -- so a restored state fails the run instead of
being measured as a product result.

